ype":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":113,"digest":"sha256:7821144b0d1517b51a9ea4fa88b81084c35d89ad54fb3f915c8887ba2f90eaef","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-11-07T19:09:21Z","updated_at":"2026-11-07T19:09:22Z"}],"body":"FluentCI v0.17.2 introduces typed module contracts, native WebAssembly components, reusable module dependencies, and Git-aware native execution. This release embeds FluentCI Engine **0.6.3**.\r\n\r\n### Modules and SDKs\r\n\r\n- **Typed named arguments and help:** Discover module functions, argument descriptions, optional fields, and return types with `--help` or `-h`. Invoke typed functions with named flags such as `--src demo`.\r\n- **Automatic signature inspection:** Generate function contracts from supported source declarations across Rust, PureScript, TypeScript, Python, Gleam, ReScript, Elixir, and ClojureScript.\r\n- **Native WebAssembly components:** Create modules with `--runtime component`. WIT interfaces and adapters are generated from code, with typed access to the SDK host capabilities. Existing Extism modules remain supported.\r\n- **Module manifests and dependencies:** Define metadata and dependencies in `fluentci-module.toml`. Use `fluentci add` and `fluentci install` to materialize dependencies into the gitignored `fluentci_modules/` directory and pin them in `fluentci.lock`.\r\n- **Composable dependency calls:** Link compatible components through their actual WIT interfaces, or call bundled Extism dependencies through scoped aliases. TypeScript component dependencies generate editor declarations for autocomplete and type checking.\r\n- **Simpler publishing:** Run `fluentci publish` directly at a module root. The module manifest supplies metadata, SDK, runtime, and dependencies without requiring `--module` or `--wasm`.\r\n\r\n### Execution and observability\r\n\r\n- **Native plan execution:** Run SDK-neutral DAG plans directly with `fluentci execute`.\r\n- **Git-aware affected selection:** Compare merge-base changes, include downstream consumers, retain required prerequisites, and declare global configuration inputs.\r\n- **Dry-run previews:** Inspect selected and omitted tasks with explanations before execution. Previewing does not run task commands, restore cached outputs, or create runtime storage.\r\n- **Incremental scheduling for cached tasks:** Cache preparation, resource waits, and retries now use the incremental ready frontier for ordinary success-dependent DAGs, while preserving wait deadlines and job limits.\r\n- **Architecture documentation:** Added `ARCHITECTURE.md` with an ASCII execution diagram, cache correctness rules, scheduler internals, measured results, and current limitations.\r\n\r\n```sh\r\nfluentci execute plan.json --affected --base origin/main --dry-run\r\nfluentci execute plan.json --affected --base origin/main --run-dir .fluentci/runs/checks\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Registry and documentation\r\n\r\n- Added publisher profiles at `/:handle` and `/:did`, with avatars, display names, distinct module totals, filtering, and infinite loading.\r\n- Author links now navigate to FluentCI publisher profiles.\r\n- Module pages show generated function documentation, typed arguments and returns, function counts, and function search.\r\n- Expanded module dependency, component, publishing, and CLI documentation, plus `/llms.txt`.\r\n\r\n### Fixes\r\n\r\n- Fixed nested Rust inspection workspaces in generated starters.\r\n- Let Spago manage PureScript compiler code generation.\r\n- Corrected the ClojureScript inspection environment and Java 21 component build requirements.\r\n- Included embedded SDK inspection assets in Nix builds.\r\n- Added OpenBSD WASI compatibility handling for unsupported TCP keepalive tuning options.\r\n\r\nRebuild existing modules with the updated SDK tooling to embed generated signatures. Native DAG dry runs do not provide a general `fluentci run --dry-run` for arbitrary module code.\r\n\r\n**Full changelog:** https://github.com/fluentci-io/fluentci/compare/v0.17.1...v0.17.2\r\n","reactions":{"total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":1,"eyes":0}}
